# Example requests. In VS Code, install the "REST Client" extension
# (by Huachao Mao), open this file, and click "Send Request" above each one.

@api = http://localhost:8080

### Create a job
POST {{api}}/v1/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: welcome-email-1

{
  "type": "send_email",
  "payload": { "to": "tisa@example.com", "subject": "Welcome" },
  "priority": 5
}

### Get a job
GET {{api}}/v1/jobs/1

### Schedule a job for later
POST {{api}}/v1/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "echo",
  "payload": { "report": "daily" },
  "run_at": "2030-01-01T09:00:00Z"
}

### A job that fails twice, then succeeds
POST {{api}}/v1/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "flaky", "payload": { "fail_attempts": 2 }, "max_attempts": 5 }

### List jobs (newest first). Use next_cursor from the response as ?before=
GET {{api}}/v1/jobs?limit=10

### Only dead jobs
GET {{api}}/v1/jobs?status=dead

### Cancel a pending job
POST {{api}}/v1/jobs/2/cancel

### Retry a dead or cancelled job
POST {{api}}/v1/jobs/2/retry

### Counts by status
GET {{api}}/v1/stats

### Live workers (needs Redis)
GET {{api}}/v1/workers

### Health and readiness
GET {{api}}/healthz

###
GET {{api}}/readyz

### Prometheus metrics (API). Worker metrics are on port 9091.
GET {{api}}/metrics
